\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af7\afs24\alang1081 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe2052\hich\af3\loch\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\ltrpar\aspalpha\cf0\f3\fs24\lang1033\kerning1\dbch\af5\langfe2052\ql{\rtlch\ai0 \ltrch\loch\i0\loch
Elizabeth sits down in a chair. \u8220\'93}{\rtlch\ai0 \ltrch\loch\i0\loch
The worker drones are very simple minded. Their minds are a bit of a empty room with a single thought suspended in it. They\u8217\'92re reactive, but essentially their motivations are to do a task until completion. In some cases I\u8217\'92ve sensed drones that are a bit more clever than the rest, but they do what they must for the hive. There\u8217\'92s no fear, only singular purpose. Queens on the other hand are a whole other thing. They\u8217\'92re quite the opposite of single minded, but it\u8217\'92s a maelstrom of competing desires. Expand the hive, keep the hive safe, find more hosts, lay more eggs. Make more drones, But all those urges competing as well as a true loathing for everything not them. They\u8217\'92re larger understanding of the universe is limited. Time isn\u8217\'92t even a concept in their minds. }{\rtlch\ai0 \ltrch\loch\i0\loch
A queen is}{\rtlch\ai0 \ltrch\loch\i0\loch
 merely an empire builder }{\rtlch\ai0 \ltrch\loch\i0\loch
of her own small empire.}{\rtlch\ai0 \ltrch\loch\i0\loch
\u8221\'94}
